# fixedbugs, defect 2117, 2026-10-17, defect 2051's shape past 4,096 bytes.
#
# SYMPTOM: `int fabs;` on a header's line past 4,096 bytes was told as clang's
# notes at the generated unit's include line, with no fix: clang quotes no
# such line, and the reader read the name under clang's caret in the line
# clang quoted.
#
# FIX: the name is read from the header's bytes (`cli/caret_bytes.hero`),
# told as C's own `fabs`, exit 1, with a `guess` fix.

extern "fixedbugs-2117-a-header-declaring-a-c-library-function-on-a-line-past-4096-bytes-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    print(eight())
